vars:pre-request {
  baseUrl: http://localhost:3000
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  # Submit ASH Weekly Attendance

  Records a weekly attendance session for the ASH after-school programme. Captures which students attended, which were mentored, the sessions conducted, volunteers present, and an optional programme review.

  On success, the attendance record is inserted into the database and cached. The endpoint returns the newly created record with a `201 Created` status.

  ## Authorization
  Requires `create` permission.

  ## Request Body (`application/json`)

  | Field                   | Type     | Required | Constraints / Allowed Values                                                           |
  |-------------------------|----------|----------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
  | sessionDate             | date     | Yes      | ISO date string — e.g. `2026-05-28` (format: `YYYY-MM-DD`)                            |
  | studentsInAttendance    | array    | Yes      | Array of valid UUIDs referencing ASH student records (min 1)                           |
  | studentsMentored        | array    | Yes      | Array of valid UUIDs referencing ASH student records (min 1)                           |
  | sessionsConducted       | array    | No       | Array of: `PERFORMANCE ART`, `SKILLS TRAINING`, `FORMATIVE TALKS` (optional)          |
  | sessionDetails          | string   | No       | Optional free text                                                                     |
  | volunteersInAttendance  | string   | Yes      | Non-empty text — names of attending volunteers                                         |
  | programReview           | string   | No       | Optional free text                                                                     |

  ## Response

  **`201 Created`** — Returns the newly created ASH weekly attendance record.

  The created record is also cached under the key `cedarrise:ash:weeklyattendance:<id>` using the `FORM_DATA` TTL.

  ## Errors

  | Status                      | Description                                                           |
  |-----------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------|
  | `400 Bad Request`           | Validation failed — missing required fields or invalid enum values.   |
  | `500 Internal Server Error` | Unexpected server error.                                              |
}
